Description: Predictive battery charging for Linux laptops
 Predictive Battery Charging (`PBC`) is a smart battery health management tool, at its core, it tries to extend the health of you devices battery by reducing the amount of time it sits at 100% by using a statistical model based on your behaviour to try and predict when your laptop charges and when it requires battery. As you use your laptop it learns about your relationship with your laptops battery and uses that information to hold back charging your device to full during certain charging sessions.
